From a318059680b8924c44510de1292adec61c4de7fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akshat Srivastava <akshat.sanya@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:37:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix build after merging full-net-and-reconnect; end turn
 automatically after the card limit

Merge fix
- RoomServer: the merge kept BOTH constructors (Taegan's reconnect grace period and the
  turn timer override) on top of each other, so the first one was never closed and the
  whole file failed. Now one constructor takes both settings; a small delegating
  constructor keeps Taegan's RoomServer(data, port, std::chrono::seconds) call working
- server_main: the merge created the server twice - now once, with the turn time
- Turn timer and reconnect pause: while a room is paused waiting for reconnects, the
  turn timer no longer ends turns; on rejoin the current turn gets a fresh timer
  (the grace period is 60 s but hero turns are 30 s, so the match kept moving)
- Timer test reads the limit from rules.json instead of expecting 60 s

New: automatic turn end
- After a hero plays maxCardsPlayedPerTurn cards (rules.json, 3) the turn ends at once
  instead of waiting for the timer; everyone is told via an info message
- The DM's turn ends after 3 card orders too, unless the final boss can still be ordered
  (that order uses no card)

Tests: card limit ends the turn at once, 1-2 cards do not; timer paused during a
reconnect pause and fresh after rejoin. Timer values in rules.json unchanged (30 / 45).
